{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender BlendFileData Structure.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender BlendFileData Structure.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender blend file data structure blender blend file data structure","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender BlendFileData Structure.md","fileName":"Blender BlendFileData Structure.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender BlendFileData Structure","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender DNA and File Loading]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender DNA and File Loading","Blender FileData Structure","Blender LibBlock Linking","Blender Context Main Assignment","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender BlendFileData Structure.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender BlendFileData Structure.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender blend file data structure blender blend file data structure","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender BlendFileData Structure.md","fileName":"Blender BlendFileData Structure.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender BlendFileData Structure","heading":"Blender BlendFileData Structure","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"`BlendFileData` is the higher-level result assembled by Blender's loader. It can carry the reconstructed `Main` database, user preferences, flags, filename information, active screen and scene pointers, the current view layer, and the recognized file type.\n\nUnlike the low-level [[Blender FileData Structure]], it represents application-ready state rather than a decoding mechanism. Once [[Blender LibBlock Linking]] has completed, setup functions use this object for [[Blender Context Main Assignment]] and related startup configuration.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender